 "note": "The kind file for schools (docs/03 ADR-36 and §18.9; kinds PR 5, S4b-BL-209): the second built-in kind, hidden behind a developer flag (web: a development build with localStorage `doorprints.dev.kinds` = `school`; the phone: a debug build made with `-Pdoorprints.devKinds=true`), so no release shows it. It proves the model with labels, hidden sections and core fields, and typed extras only: no screen of its own. The school's own money is hidden (the fees are extras with fixed cadences: `year`, the figure schools quote, and `once` for the admission fee), and so are the broker, the rooms, the questions, the viewings, moving in and the checklist. Its question seed is the shared bank, unused while `questions` is hidden. Labels are keys (web: web/src/app/i18n, Android: android/ui/src/commonMain/composeResources); school-vectors.json pins what they resolve to in en, hi, ta and te. No `was`: no school was ever stored in the backup family before the reset. The `ai` slots are read since kinds PR 7 (S4b-BL-211, docs/03 §18.11), while the developer flag is on: `extract` is what *Fill in from listing text* fills (not `commuteMinutes`, the person's own measure, which no listing states), `ask` is every line of an Ask document in its order (core fields, the extras by their English words, and the sections `areaNotes`, `distances` and `visits`), `plan` is what the Plan tools show and filter on (S4b-BL-270: the core fields it names and the extras it names, so a planner can pick schools with a bus; the admission fee only in `houseDetails`, which reads `ask`), and `never` wins over every other slot. An extra no slot names, and an extra the kind does not know, never reaches a provider; kind-ai-vectors.json pins the lines.",
